# Linear MCP Protocol

## Scope

- Use only team/project scope from `.ai/linear-scope.json` when the file is present.
- Do not mix issues from foreign teams or unrelated projects.

## Tracker contract

- `linear.enabled`: `{{ "true" if linear_enabled else "false" }}`
- `linear.requireTrackerForIssueFlow`: `{{ "true" if linear_require_tracker else "false" }}`
- Current workflow tracker: `{{ workflow_tracker }}`

## Allowed operations

- get issue
- update issue state
- create issue
- list issues
- list issue statuses
- create comment (general discussion and acceptance evidence, without duplicating OpenSpec bodies)

## Planning / execution storage

- Canonical planning lives in the selected OpenSpec change; orchestrator execution state lives in run JSON.
- Do not copy entire OpenSpec artifacts into Linear comments.

## Stop / degraded mode

{% if linear_enabled %}
- If Linear MCP is unavailable and the step needs a **workflow state** change, stop or enter degraded mode explicitly; continue with OpenSpec and run JSON and report pending state sync.
- OpenSpec remains the planning source of truth; do not mirror its full body into Linear when connectivity returns.
{% else %}
- Linear is not enabled by default for this profile.
- If the team wants Linear-first workflow, fill `.ai/linear-scope.json`, enable the plugin in `.cursor/settings.json`, and wire MCP locally.
{% endif %}

## Runtime states

- For tracker-first flows:
  - plan becomes implement-ready -> move to `{{ tracker_status_plan_ready }}`
  - execution starts -> move to `{{ tracker_status_active }}`
  - review-ready state -> move to `{{ tracker_status_review }}`
- In degraded mode, keep tracker sync pending until connectivity is restored.
